# @NAME@

<!-- package-context -->
This guide describes the current source, including unreleased changes.
<!-- /package-context -->

`@NAME@` is a short installation and import name for
[CelestialCalendar](https://github.com/0xf3cd/celestial-calendar), an astronomy and Chinese calendar library.
It installs the exact same version of `celestial-calendar` and forwards its public top-level Python API.

```sh
python -m pip install @NAME@
```

```python
import @NAME@ as astro

lunar = astro.gregorian_to_lunar(astro.LunarAlgorithm.ALGO2, astro.GregorianDate(2024, 2, 10))
print(lunar)
```

The functions, types and exceptions are the original `celestial_calendar` objects. You can install `cele`,
`wentian` and `celestial-calendar` together at the same version. Use `celestial_calendar` for submodule imports.

See the [Python guide](https://0xf3cd.github.io/celestial-calendar/bindings/python/README.html) for supported
platforms, examples and API details. This alias adds no native implementation and has the same platform
requirements as its dependency.
